<BaseLayout title="Submit" description="Submit fiction, poetry, essays, criticism, translation, art and photography to The Scandinavian Quarterly by email.">
<article class="standard-page"><header class="page-heading wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Contribute to the magazine</p><h1>Submit your work</h1><p class="standfirst">TSQ accepts submissions directly by email.</p></header><div class="gh-content"><div class="email-panel"><p class="eyebrow">Submission address</p><a class="email-address" href="mailto:submissions@thescandinavianquarterly.com?subject=TSQ%20Submission">submissions@thescandinavianquarterly.com</a><p>Put the category of your submission in the subject line. Please read the full guidelines before sending work.</p><div class="inline-actions"><a class="button" href="/submission-guidelines/">Read full guidelines</a><a class="read-link" href="mailto:submissions@thescandinavianquarterly.com?subject=TSQ%20Submission">Open your email app</a></div></div><div class="submission-policy-panel"><p class="eyebrow">Response time &amp; publication history</p><p>We aim to respond to submissions within <strong>48 hours</strong>. Please tell us in your email whether the work has been published before, and if so, where it first appeared.</p><p>Previously published work is welcome for publication on the TSQ website if you retain the necessary rights. <strong>Only work first published by TSQ is eligible for our issue compilations.</strong></p></div>
<h2>What we read</h2><div class="guideline-grid">
<section><h3>Poetry</h3><p>Poetry from Nordic writers and poets elsewhere whose work meaningfully engages with the Nordic region, languages, cultures or literary traditions.</p><a class="read-link" href="mailto:submissions@thescandinavianquarterly.com?subject=Poetry%20Submission">Email poetry</a></section>
<section><h3>Fiction</h3><p>Short fiction and narrative work with a clear literary or cultural fit for TSQ.</p><a class="read-link" href="mailto:submissions@thescandinavianquarterly.com?subject=Fiction%20Submission">Email fiction</a></section>
<section><h3>Essays &amp; Criticism</h3><p>Literary essays, criticism, cultural writing, reviews and reported or reflective nonfiction.</p><a class="read-link" href="mailto:submissions@thescandinavianquarterly.com?subject=Essay%20or%20Criticism%20Submission">Email an essay</a></section>
<section><h3>Translation</h3><p>Literary translation from English into a Nordic language, from a Nordic language into English, or from one Nordic language into another. Include translator credit and any permissions required for the original work.</p><a class="read-link" href="mailto:submissions@thescandinavianquarterly.com?subject=Translation%20Submission">Email translation</a></section>
<section><h3>Art &amp; Photography</h3><p>Original visual work, photo essays, documentary photography and artwork suitable for digital publication.</p><a class="read-link" href="mailto:submissions@thescandinavianquarterly.com?subject=Art%20or%20Photography%20Submission">Email art or photography</a></section>
</div><p class="static-notice"><strong>Please note:</strong> TSQ is online-only. Accepted work is published on our website. Work first published by TSQ may also be selected for an issue compilation; reprints are not included in issue compilations.</p></div></article>
</BaseLayout>
